# PART 2 — AI CARE & FEEDBACK LEARNING

## 2.1 Improve recommendation context

Update the existing Gemini AI Care context builder to use the new analytics where permitted.

The recommendation context may include:

- Existing Energy Index.
- Sleep trends.
- RHR deviations from personal baseline.
- HRV deviations from personal baseline.
- HRV measurement type.
- Activity patterns.
- Self-reported energy.
- User's explicitly stated care preferences.
- Previous feedback.
- Completed Care History.
- Weekly Couple Recharge preferences, if shared.

The statistical layer must calculate all metrics.

Gemini should explain the supplied evidence and generate optional care suggestions.

Gemini must not invent statistics, calculate medical conclusions, or diagnose health conditions.

Do not infer emotions from sleep, HRV, or heart rate.

Every recommendation must include:

- Recommendation Title.
- Description.
- Why This Fits.
- Suggested Time.
- Send Care.
- Save Suggestion.

Every generated recommendation set should include at least one practical non-purchase action.

Examples:

- Send a Gentle Check-in.
- Plan a Quiet Evening.
- Prepare a Warm Drink.
- Give Your Partner Some Rest Time.
- Suggest a Relaxing Shared Activity.

Do not make AI Care a shopping recommendation engine.

## 2.2 Separate sender actions and receiver feedback

Implement a clear feedback model.

Sender actions:
- Sent.
- Saved.
- Skipped.

Receiver feedback:
- Helpful.
- Not Helpful.
- Not Suitable for Me.

Do not treat sender preference as equivalent to receiver preference.

Store feedback with:

- Recommendation ID.
- Sender ID.
- Recipient ID.
- Action.
- Feedback.
- Timestamp.
- Recommendation category.

Update the existing Feedback Learning mechanism.

For the current Demo, use local data and deterministic rule-based recommendation ranking.

Repeated positive receiver feedback should gradually increase the priority of similar recommendation categories.

Negative feedback should reduce their priority.

Avoid extreme preference changes from a single response.

The interface should explain that the system learns from user feedback, not that a new AI model is being trained.

## 2.3 Saved Suggestions

